  "title": "Replace react-redux with in-house Provider and hooks",
  "body": "> Related to #5552.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Changed\n\n- Removed the `react-redux` dependency, which conflicted with React 19 as a peer dependency, related to [#5552](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/issues/5552), in PR [#5964](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5964), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\n`react-redux@7.2.9` requires React 16.8–18 as a peer dependency, so installing Web Chat with React 19 warns and fails with `--strict-peer-deps`. Web Chat only used its `Provider` and three hooks on an internal context, which are now implemented in-house with the same behavior, and `react-redux` is removed from `api` and `component`.\n\n## Design\n\n- Not upgrading `react-redux`: 8 still caps React at 18, 9 requires React 18 or later.\n- `useSelector()` re-renders through `useReducer()` like `react-redux@7`, not `useSyncExternalStore()` (`react-redux@8`/`use-sync-external-store`): on React 18 it re-renders ahead of `<GraphProvider>`'s `useState()` and the development check in `useActivities()` throws (e.g. `selectedAction.html`).\n- Store notifications to all hooks run in one `unstable_batchedUpdates()`, as `react-redux@7` does, so React 16/17 and `ReactDOM.render()` re-render parent and child together.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `WebChatReduxContext.ts`: `useSelector(selector, equalityFn)`, `useDispatch()`, `useStore()` replacing the `react-redux` hook factories\n- `WebChatReduxProvider.tsx`: provides the store and a batched `subscribe()`, used by `<Composer>`\n- `WebChatReduxProvider.spec.tsx`: parent and child re-render once together, `equalityFn` skips re-renders, dispatching in render re-renders once\n- `api`, `component`: removed `react-redux` from `package.json`\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
